I looked at several distributions in the
NIST Engineering Statistics Handbook.
An exponential distribution can model how long it takes
for the next customer to arrive.
A Poisson distribution can model how many customers
arrive in an hour.
Both examples assume customers arrive independently
at a steady average rate.
A uniform distribution could model a service time
between 2 and 6 minutes if any one-minute interval
in that range is equally likely.
A normal distribution could model measurement errors
that are usually close to zero.
A binomial distribution could model how many out of 20
customers buy something if each customer independently has the same chance of buying.